WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.016
A signal graph puts time on the horizontal axis and amplitude on the vertical axis. This 100 hertz sine spans 20 milliseconds.

2
00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:13.809
The same axis can be read in seconds: 20 milliseconds are two hundredths of a second.

3
00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:22.296
In digital audio it is also read as sample number. At 8000 samples per second, the same 20 milliseconds are 160 samples.

4
00:00:22.998 --> 00:00:29.036
The conversion is a single formula: the time of sample n is n divided by the sampling rate.

5
00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:36.600
One hertz is one cycle per second. One hundred hertz are one hundred cycles in a second; two cycles fit in 20 milliseconds.
